ui.projectbee:info.advance_beehive=§eAdvanced Beehive§r\nAn automated beehive that collects bee\nproducts and produces honeycombs.\n\n§bBee Input§r — Insert a filled bee cage\n§bBee Storage§r — Stores up to 5 working bees\n§bCatalyst Slot§r — Insert required catalyst\n§bOutput Grid§r — Collect produced items\n§bUpgrade Slots§r — Install machine upgrades\n\n§7Tip:§r Place an §fExtension Box§r above or\nbelow to expand bee storage to 7 slots.
ui.projectbee:info.advance_beehive_expanded=§eAdvanced Beehive (Expanded)§r\nExpanded beehive with additional storage.\n\n§bBee Input§r — Insert a filled bee cage\n§bBee Storage§r — Stores up to 7 working bees\n§bCatalyst Slot§r — Insert required catalyst\n§bOutput Grid§r — Collect produced items\n§bUpgrade Slots§r — Install machine upgrades
ui.projectbee:info.breeding_chamber=§eBreeding Chamber§r\nBreeds two compatible bees to produce\na new offspring species.\n\n§bCage Slots§r — Insert two filled bee cages\n§bFlower Slots§r — Insert matching flowers\n§bOutput§r — Collect baby bee cages\n\n§7Note:§r Cages are not consumed.\n§7One flower per slot is consumed each cycle.
ui.projectbee:info.bee_incubator=§eBee Incubator§r\nGrows baby bees into adults using\nHoney Treats and energy.\n\n§bInput§r — Baby filled bee cage\n§bOutput§r — Adult filled bee cage\n§bHoney Treats§r — Consumed per process\n\n§7Treat cost by bee tier:§r\n §aCommon§r — 1 treat\n §aSemi-Rare§r — 2–3 treats\n §aRare§r — 4 treats\n §aLegendary§r — 5–6 treats
ui.projectbee:info.centrifuge=§eCentrifuge§r\nProcesses honeycombs into raw materials.\n\n§bInput§r — Insert a honeycomb\n§bOutput Grid§r — Collect processed items
ui.projectbee:info.powered_centrifuge=§ePowered Centrifuge§r\nEnergy-powered centrifuge with faster\nprocessing than the basic model.\n\n§bInput§r — Insert a honeycomb\n§bOutput Grid§r — Collect processed items\n\n§7Requires §aDE§7 per operation.
ui.projectbee:info.feeding_slab=§eFeeding Slab§r\nHolds food items for the Advanced Beehive\nwhen a Simulator Upgrade is installed.\n\n§bSlots§r — Place food blocks or items\n\n§7Tip:§r Right-click with another Feeding Slab\nto double the storage capacity.
ui.projectbee:info.feeding_slab_double=§eFeeding Slab (Double)§r\nExpanded feeding slab with 6 storage slots.\n\n§bSlots§r — Place food blocks or items

