## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## HOW TO PLAY — INTRODUCTION SECTION
## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

howtoplay.pb.introduction.p1=§eProject Bee§r is a bee management and automation addon built as an extension of §6UtilityCraft§r.\n\nIt adds custom bee species, specialised machines, and a progression system that lets you collect resources passively through your bees.

howtoplay.pb.introduction.h1=Getting Started

howtoplay.pb.introduction.p2=To catch a bee you need a §bBee Cage§r. Right-click any bee with an empty cage to fill it. A §bSturdy Bee Cage§r is reusable — the cage returns to you when you release the bee.\n\nPlace a filled cage into the §bAdvanced Beehive§r to put the bee to work.

howtoplay.pb.introduction.h2=Comb Processing

howtoplay.pb.introduction.p3=Every bee produces a specific §bcomb§r type. Combs are collected from the Advanced Beehive's output grid and processed in the §bCentrifuge§r or §bPowered Centrifuge§r to extract raw materials such as ores, gems, ingots, and special drops.

howtoplay.pb.introduction.h3=Upgrades

howtoplay.pb.introduction.p4=The Advanced Beehive accepts §bSpeed Upgrade§r modules (Tiers I–V) in its upgrade slots to increase processing speed. Install a §bSimulator Upgrade§r to run the hive without live bees — feed it items via a §bFeeding Slab§r placed above or below.

## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## HOW TO PLAY — BEES SECTION
## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

howtoplay.pb.bees.intro=Project Bee works with two groups of bees: §6UtilityCraft bees§r (custom species) and §aMinecraft bees§r (vanilla). Both can be caught, bred, and housed in the Advanced Beehive.

howtoplay.pb.bees.h_uc_bees=UtilityCraft Bees

howtoplay.pb.bees.p_uc_bees=These species are added by the UtilityCraft ecosystem and each produce a unique resource comb:\n\n§7Ore bees:§r Iron · Copper · Gold · Coal · Redstone · Lapis · Quartz · Netherite · Duranium\n§7Gem bees:§r Diamond · Emerald · Amethyst · Echo · Ender\n§7Special bees:§r Slime · Obsidian · Bone · Glowing · Magmatic · Biomass\n§7Alloy bees:§r Steel · Energized Iron · Voltanium · Adamant\n§7Nature bees:§r Bumble · Leaf Cutter · Blue Banded · Blue Mason · Magnetic · Mining · Dirt\n\n[Photo — UC bee showcase]

howtoplay.pb.bees.h_mc_bees=Minecraft Bees

howtoplay.pb.bees.p_mc_bees=The standard vanilla §eBee§r is fully compatible with Project Bee machines. Catch it with a Bee Cage, house it in the Advanced Beehive, and it produces regular §eHoneycomb§r.\n\n§7Centrifuge output:§r Honeycomb → §aWax§r (99%)\n\n[Photo — Minecraft bee]

## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## HOW TO PLAY — MACHINES SECTION
## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

howtoplay.pb.machines.intro=All Project Bee machines are listed here. Energy machines run on §eDE (Dorios Energy)§r from the UtilityCraft energy system.

howtoplay.pb.machines.h_advance_beehive=Advanced Beehive

howtoplay.pb.machines.p_advance_beehive=The core machine of Project Bee. Houses up to §b5 working bees§r and automatically collects their comb output.\n\n§bBee Input§r — Insert a filled Bee Cage\n§bBee Storage§r — 5 bee slots (7 with Extension Box)\n§bCatalyst Slot§r — Insert the required catalyst for your bees\n§bOutput Grid§r — 3×3 grid; collect combs and other products here\n§bUpgrade Slots§r — Speed Upgrade I–V or Simulator Upgrade

howtoplay.pb.machines.h_breeding_chamber=Breeding Chamber

howtoplay.pb.machines.p_breeding_chamber=Combines two bee species to produce a §bbaby bee offspring§r.\n\n§bCage Slots§r — Insert two filled Bee Cages (cages are §lnot§r consumed)\n§bFlower Slots§r — Insert the matching flowers; §cone flower consumed per cycle§r\n§bOutput§r — Baby filled Bee Cage\n\n§7Compatibility depends on the two parent species.

howtoplay.pb.machines.h_bee_incubator=Bee Incubator

howtoplay.pb.machines.p_bee_incubator=Grows a §bbaby bee§r into an §badult§r using energy and Honey Treats.\n\n§bInput§r — Baby filled Bee Cage\n§bOutput§r — Adult filled Bee Cage\n§bHoney Treats§r — Consumed each cycle\n\n§7Treat cost by tier:§r Common §a1§r · Semi-Rare §a2–3§r · Rare §a4§r · Legendary §a5–6§r

howtoplay.pb.machines.h_centrifuge=Centrifuge

howtoplay.pb.machines.p_centrifuge=A manual centrifuge that processes §bhoneycombs§r into raw materials. No energy required — good for early-game use.\n\n§bInput§r — Insert a honeycomb\n§bOutput Grid§r — 3×3 result grid

howtoplay.pb.machines.h_powered_centrifuge=Powered Centrifuge

howtoplay.pb.machines.p_powered_centrifuge=An energy-powered centrifuge with faster processing than the basic model.\n\n§bInput§r — Insert a honeycomb\n§bOutput Grid§r — 3×3 result grid\n§eRequires DE§r per operation\n\n§7Each comb yields different outputs. Common drops: raw ores/ingots (50%), §aWax§r (99%).

howtoplay.pb.machines.h_feeding_slab=Feeding Slab

howtoplay.pb.machines.p_feeding_slab=Holds food items for the Advanced Beehive when a §bSimulator Upgrade§r is installed.\n\n§bSlots§r — 3 food storage slots\n§7Place directly above or below the Advanced Beehive.\n§7Tip:§r Right-click a placed Feeding Slab with another to merge into a §fDouble Feeding Slab§r (6 slots).

howtoplay.pb.machines.h_extension_box=Extension Box

howtoplay.pb.machines.p_extension_box=Expands the Advanced Beehive's bee storage from §b5 to 7 slots§r.\n\n§7Place directly §labove§r or §lbelow§r an Advanced Beehive to activate.\nNo energy or configuration required — links automatically.

